# Jev Router settings. Copy this file and fill in your key; never commit the copy.
#
# 1. Get a Jev API key from TypeSafe: sign in at https://console.typesafe.ai and create a key
#    on the API keys page, https://console.typesafe.ai/keys
#
# 2. Put this file where jev-claude will find it, then paste your key below. The installer
#    (install.sh or install.ps1) does this for you and asks for the key.
#
#    For every project (recommended):
#      macOS / Linux:       cp .env.example ~/.jev-router.env
#      Windows PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example "$HOME\.jev-router.env"
#
#    For one project only: copy or rename it to .env in the directory you start jev-claude
#    from (already ignored by git here). A project's .env may only set the JEV_* settings in
#    this file, never anything that could redirect traffic.
#
# 3. Start jev-claude. The first launch offers a setup check that confirms routing is on.

# Required: paste your key straight after the =. TYPESAFE_API_KEY also works.
JEV_API_KEY=

# ---- Optional: remove the leading # to change a setting ----

# Run Claude Code on an Anthropic API key instead of your Claude subscription sign-in. Usage is
# then billed per token to the key's account. Create a key in the Claude Console,
# https://platform.claude.com. Claude Code asks once, in its first session, whether to use it.
# Set this only here in ~/.jev-router.env or in your shell: a project's .env cannot set it, so a
# cloned repository can never send your work to someone else's account.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Fable, the most capable and most expensive tier, is offered by default for long-horizon
# work and adversarial reviews. It bills extra usage credits. Set to 0 to turn it off.
# JEV_ALLOW_FABLE=0

# Reasoning effort for a tier, used only when Claude Code sends none (it normally sends its
# own). One of: low, medium, high, xhigh, max.
# JEV_SONNET_EFFORT=high
# JEV_OPUS_EFFORT=medium
# JEV_FABLE_EFFORT=high

# Log each routing decision to ~/.jev-claude.log.
# JEV_DEBUG=1

# Turn off the Jev status line in Claude Code.
# JEV_NO_STATUSLINE=1
